## OWASP Top 10 Checklist

| Risk | Mitigation |
|------|------------|
| **Injection** | Parameterized queries, input validation |
| **Broken Auth** | Strong passwords, MFA, session management |
| **Sensitive Data** | Encryption, HTTPS, proper headers |
| **XXE** | Disable DTD processing |
| **Broken Access** | Authorization checks, RBAC |
| **Security Misconfig** | Helmet, proper defaults |
| **XSS** | Output encoding, CSP, sanitization |
| **Insecure Deserialization** | Input validation, avoid eval |
| **Vulnerable Components** | Dependency scanning |
| **Logging/Monitoring** | Security logging, alerting |

## Production Checklist

```typescript
// src/shared/security/audit.ts

export function securityAudit(): string[] {
  const issues: string[] = [];

  // Check environment
  if (process.env.NODE_ENV !== "production") {
    issues.push("NODE_ENV is not set to production");
  }

  // Check secrets
  if (process.env.JWT_SECRET?.length < 32) {
    issues.push("JWT_SECRET should be at least 32 characters");
  }

  // Check HTTPS
  if (!process.env.FORCE_HTTPS) {
    issues.push("HTTPS should be enforced");
  }

  // Check rate limiting
  if (!process.env.REDIS_URL) {
    issues.push("Redis recommended for distributed rate limiting");
  }

  return issues;
}
```

## Conventions

- Use Helmet for security headers
- Configure CORS explicitly (never use `*` in production)
- Implement rate limiting on all endpoints
- Use CSRF protection for cookie-based auth
- Validate and sanitize all input
- Use parameterized queries only
- Store secrets in environment variables
- Log security events
- Keep dependencies updated
- Use HTTPS everywhere

## Anti-Patterns

- ❌ Using `cors({ origin: "*" })` in production
- ❌ Missing rate limiting
- ❌ Storing secrets in code
- ❌ Disabling security headers
- ❌ String concatenation in SQL queries
- ❌ Missing CSRF protection
- ❌ Not validating input
- ❌ Ignoring dependency vulnerabilities
- ❌ Exposing stack traces in production
- ❌ Missing security logging

**See also:** `auth.mdc`, `input-sanitization.mdc`, `validation.mdc`, `../../patterns/security.mdc`
